The business should ensure that there are a sufficient number of food vendors that can cook and serve adequate amounts of healthy and hygienic meals to all workers

remediation_business_steps_taken:
Business; 
Issara raised this issue with the business, the business responded that it was the rejection from the government side for several reasons such as workers being suspected of using a fake passport, workers failing fingerprint, workers being reported as runaway workers by their former employers which caused them not getting their permit approved as submitted. The business tried doing an appeal, however, they were still rejected by the immigration. Therefore, the business was asked by immigration to repatriate them immediately. 

Issara;
Issara shared this update with several workers, they added that it was too short notice for them, if the business has informed them about their attempt through the appeal process, workers may have prepared for this departure. Since it was an unexpected dismissal, several workers are facing financial and mental issues such as (uncertainty about their future, feeling pressured to go back to Myanmar, and so on). 

Thandar Linn; 
She reported that in her case, she was not invited for any fingerprint or is using a fake passport, therefore, she thinks the business should conduct more investigation for her.

Business; 
The business's current HR checked the recording system and also with the former HR, the former Hr responded to the current HR that her case was about having a fake passport(the business that is issued it under her sister's name). Therefore, she was rejected by immigration. 

Workers; 

She said that she is aware of that fake issue that is happening to her colleague but not her. For her, Thandar Linn is her real name and she had never been invited to do a fingerprint.

Business; 
The business responded, that they never charge workers any recruitment fees. For the workers that were recruited under the "Recalibration Program" were handled by the runner that Ramatex has. If there are any workers who want to leave the job, Triston is the one who signs the resignation. Triston so far has not received any resignation letter that needs his signature from Blueberry and Blueberry is the factory that has lest turnover rate. If workers want to leave the job, they can just fill out the resignation simply and the rest process will be handled by HR and other relevant teams. Triston will do his own internal investigation making sure safeguard for the worker is in place. 

The document process is taking longer than expected from the government side, the government has announced it to finalize the processes at the end of this year.

Worker; 

The worker reported to Issara that she was invited by HR to be communicated about the process of resignation and to collect her passport from the immigration as it was there for the legalization process. The worker added that she was told not to have to pay for her documents as previously asked by one of the HR. 

Business; 
Triston from HR responded saying that he has visited the Blueberry site to very some of the highlights about this issue and also has checked with other facilities to make sure everything is aligned. 


Worker; 
The worker updated that she had to go to immigration to collect her passport and now the passport is with her. She also added that there was another Nepalese worker who also went to the immigration to collect his passport. It is added that many Nepalese workers are planning to resign from Blueberry. She said that she also received her remaining salary which is 800 MYR from the business which she did not expect to receive before Issara's involvement to raise her case with the business. 







CLOSURE NOTE; 

Issara raised this issue with the business, the business responded that they never charge any fees from workers for the document process, therefore the business agreed to conduct the investigation. Several days later, the worker confirmed being communicated by HR about her document status that had been submitted to immigration for legalization. The worker was also informed about the employer pay recruitment policy that is being practiced by the company and brought to the immigration to collect her passport. The worker confirmed receiving her passport and remaining wages. However, it was challenging for Issara's team to get a comprehensive response from HR in a timely manner. Issara followed up with the business a few times, but the business only responded by saying that they have checked some of the highlights in a certain facility and also check all remaining facilities to make sure everything is aligned. It is unclear from the business side about the investigation result and the action being taken towards relevant staff that was charging money from workers.
